{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Module Creation Assistant",
  "description": "Automatically generates module scaffolding including lifecycle hooks, display hooks, and placeholder methods when a new module folder or main PHP file is created",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "modules/*/",
      "modules/*/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A new module has been detected. Please analyze the module structure and generate the following:\n\n1. **Module Lifecycle Methods**: Generate stubbed install(), uninstall(), enable(), disable() methods with proper return statements and basic error handling\n\n2. **Hook Registrations**: Pre-populate registerHook() calls for common hotel management hooks like:\n   - displayHeader, displayFooter\n   - actionBookingCreate, actionBookingUpdate\n   - displayRoomDetails, displayBookingForm\n   - actionCustomerAccountAdd\n   - displayAdminOrder\n\n3. **Hook Implementation Methods**: Create placeholder hook methods with proper naming convention (hookDisplayHeader, hookActionValidateOrder, etc.) including:\n   - Parameter validation comments\n   - Return value examples\n   - Common use case comments\n\n4. **Configuration Methods**: Add getContent() method for module configuration with basic form structure\n\n5. **Database Methods**: Add createTables() and dropTables() placeholder methods for database operations\n\n6. **Module Metadata**: Ensure proper module constructor with name, version, author, description, and compatibility settings\n\nPlease generate clean, well-commented PHP code following QloApps module development standards and include proper error handling and validation patterns."
  }
}